  <div class="tag">Decision Authority Research &mdash; AI Governance</div>

  <h1>AI Governance for Irreversible Decisions</h1>
  <p class="header-sub">When a model acts faster than governance can respond, who is named to stop it?</p>
  <p class="header-def">Named stop authority for autonomous systems, agentic AI, and production deployments.</p>

  <div class="core-principle">
    <div class="core-label">The core problem</div>
    <div class="core-text">
      Agentic AI does not create the accountability gap.<br>
      It exposes it at scale.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="scenarios">

    <div class="scenario">
      <div class="scenario-inner">
        <div class="scenario-index">Scenario 01 &mdash; Production deployment</div>
        <div class="scenario-title">A model is approved and deployed. Harm begins before governance responds.</div>
        <p class="scenario-body">An AI model reaches 40,000 users before outputs are reviewed. Behavior deviates from expected parameters. The team escalates. By the time an emergency meeting is scheduled, the exposure is already at scale.</p>
        <div class="scenario-gap"><strong>The gap:</strong> No named individual had real-time authority to halt the deployment. The approval existed. The stop did not.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="scenario">
      <div class="scenario-inner">
        <div class="scenario-index">Scenario 02 &mdash; Autonomous agent action</div>
        <div class="scenario-title">An agentic system executes a sequence of actions. No human override was defined.</div>
        <p class="scenario-body">An autonomous agent is authorized to act within defined parameters. It encounters an edge case and continues executing. The action cannot be undone. No individual was named in advance to interrupt the sequence.</p>
        <div class="scenario-gap"><strong>The gap:</strong> Human override was assumed to exist. It was never assigned to a name.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="scenario">
      <div class="scenario-inner">
        <div class="scenario-index">Scenario 03 &mdash; Model rollback impossible</div>
        <div class="scenario-title">A model update propagates. Rollback requires a decision no one is authorized to make alone.</div>
        <p class="scenario-body">A production model update causes unexpected outputs across multiple downstream systems. Rollback is technically possible but requires authorization. The team cannot identify who has individual authority to approve it. Time passes. Damage accumulates.</p>
        <div class="scenario-gap"><strong>The gap:</strong> Rollback authority was distributed across functions. No single person was named and pre-committed.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <div class="why-now">
    <div class="why-label">Why this is urgent now</div>
    <div class="why-item"><span class="why-dash">&#8212;</span>EU AI Act Article 9 requires human oversight mechanisms for high-risk AI systems</div>
    <div class="why-item"><span class="why-dash">&#8212;</span>Agentic systems act, plan, and optimize without waiting for committee approval</div>
    <div class="why-item"><span class="why-dash">&#8212;</span>Release cycles are accelerating while stop authority remains undefined</div>
    <div class="why-item"><span class="why-dash">&#8212;</span>When harm occurs, regulators and boards ask for a name, not a process</div>
  </div>

  <div class="what-dar">
    <div class="what-label">What a DAR engagement delivers for AI governance</div>
    <div class="what-items">
      <div class="what-item"><span class="what-n">01</span><div class="what-text"><strong>Named stop authority per deployment pathway</strong>One individual defined, in writing, before release.</div></div>
      <div class="what-item"><span class="what-n">02</span><div class="what-text"><strong>Human override mapping</strong>Who can halt the system before actions become irreversible.</div></div>
      <div class="what-item"><span class="what-n">03</span><div class="what-text"><strong>Escalation gap analysis</strong>Where escalation paths exist without a named decision owner.</div></div>
      <div class="what-item"><span class="what-n">04</span><div class="what-text"><strong>Formal Decision Authority Record</strong>Written. Named. Pre-committed. Before deployment.</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="closing">
    <div class="closing-q">Before your next AI deployment:<br>who, by name, can stop it if it needs to be stopped?</div>
    <div class="closing-a">If the answer is unclear, distributed, or delayed &mdash; accountability has already failed.</div>
